  "model_selection_rationale": "Logistic Regression with Sigmoid Platt calibration achieves the lowest fold-mean Brier score (0.2060) and lowest fold-mean ECE (0.1000) with robust discrimination (ROC-AUC 0.716, PR-AUC 0.610). At standard threshold 0.50, probability compression on this minority class causes sensitivity collapse (Recall 31.2%, F1 0.403). Operating threshold 0.35 (derived from the sigmoid-calibrated model's inner-OOF distribution: mean 0.319, range 0.20\u20130.37; distinct from uncalibrated LR mean 0.303) resolves probability compression, lifting sensitivity to 79.5% \u00b1 10.7% and F1 to 0.604 \u00b1 0.051."
